        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix stylesheet glossary]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43475</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43475"/>
        <updated>2026-03-17T12:27:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/259028460?u=76c93f0df0fbeb4706736acca78f07a43e398a63&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43427.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4069573538" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43427" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43427/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43427">#43427</a></p>
<p dir="auto">This PR clarifies the terminology used for "stylesheet" in the glossary.</p>
<p dir="auto">MDN commonly uses the one-word form "stylesheet", while official specifications such as those from the W3C use the two-word form "style sheet".</p>
<p dir="auto">This update keeps MDN’s convention while acknowledging both forms to improve clarity and consistency.</p>]]></content>
