    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF149 @container style() allows but ignores !important]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43466</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43466"/>
        <updated>2026-03-17T03:30:06.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This updated does two things.</p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Updates the "Using container size and style queries" doc to:
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Update legacy note that only style queries with custom properties are supported. I believe all the types are - certainly that is what the <code class="notranslate">@container</code> docs indicate and the BCD seems to show.</li>
<li>Link the Container style queries intro to the more detailed section on <code class="notranslate">@container</code> doc.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Adds a note in <code class="notranslate">@container</code> docs that <code class="notranslate">!important</code> is allowed in style queries but ignored. This apparently is not clear in the spec but is in a <a href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-conditional/container-queries/at-container-style-parsing.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned" rel="nofollow">WPT test that is passed by all browsers</a>. This came up in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2014095" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2014095</a> and I think is worthy of a mention.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3978087686" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43216" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43216/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43216">#43216</a></p>]]></content>
